It is an independent re-implementation of the training recipe described in
"SweRank: Software Issue Localization with Code Ranking" (Reddy et al., arXiv 2505.07849).
No SweRank code or model weights were used for training, filtering or mining; the method was implemented from
the paper text. SweRankEmbed-Small (CC-BY-NC-4.0) was only evaluated as a reference.

Third-party code included:

- third_party/cornstack/: copied unmodified (apart from a header) from
  https://github.com/gangiswag/cornstack (commit c4f3e1289df917275860affc03e640ddf99d466f),
  Apache License 2.0, Copyright the CoRNStack authors. Used only to reproduce the
  SWE-Bench-Lite function-localization evaluation protocol. Those files are themselves derived
  from Agentless (https://github.com/OpenAutoCoder/Agentless), MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2024 OpenAutoCoder. Licence texts: third_party/cornstack/LICENSE.cornstack-Apache-2.0 and
  third_party/cornstack/LICENSE.agentless-MIT.

Models and data:

- Base model: nomic-ai/CodeRankEmbed (MIT License).
- Training tasks: nebius/SWE-rebench and nebius/SWE-rebench-V2 (CC-BY-4.0; Badertdinov et al.,
  arXiv 2505.20411, and "SWE-rebench V2", arXiv 2602.23866), restricted to
  repositories with permissive licences (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Unlicense, CC0, ...). No code or issue text from the training
  or evaluation repositories is included in this repository; see docs/DATA.md for the pointer format and build script. The pointer
  file (data/train_pointers.parquet) is adapted from SWE-rebench / SWE-rebench-V2 (row selection, derived function
  ids) and is distributed under CC-BY-4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
- Evaluation labels: czlll/SWE-bench_Lite (gold functions released with LocAgent) over
  princeton-nlp/SWE-bench_Lite (SWE-bench code is MIT; the HF dataset card declares no licence).
- Second evaluation set: czlll/Loc-Bench_V1 (LocAgent, Chen et al., arXiv 2503.09089; the HF dataset card
  declares no licence), used for evaluation only and not redistributed.
